b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd reverse that, make the &quot;Beast&quot; a Hunter Heart (the beast part) Fairest (the Prince part).</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not understand - could you point those in the books? Also, we talk here about dynamics of Seemings in the 2ED where character can &quot;evolve&quot; under the guise of Wyrd.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T14:52:45-08:00","id":793278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/792605-2ed-seemings-and-fairytales?p=793184#post793184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not understand - could you point those in the books? Also, we talk here about dynamics of Seemings in the 2ED where character can &quot;evolve&quot; under the guise of Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fairest is seeming, hunter heart is a kith, both have been converted to 2e. Though I do find it strange you turned the seeming into a punishment inflicted on the changeling, since that is meant to be the kith aspect in 2e not the seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T22:59:00-08:00","id":793446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/792605-2ed-seemings-and-fairytales?p=793278#post793278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fairest is seeming, hunter heart is a kith, both have been converted to 2e. Though I do find it strange you turned the seeming into a punishment inflicted on the changeling, since that is meant to be the kith aspect in 2e not the seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because only &quot;curse&quot; way have logic in this story. Prince <i><b>wants to stop being</b></i> Beast - it's fundamental to this fairytale. The 2ED Seemings are this way weird, now - they are <b>totally</b> contrary to the fairytales they are based on.<br /> <br /> Prince IS of &quot;Prince Kith&quot;, as it is his original role, in first narrative - in his narrative only change was he become Beast Seeming - and only under the curse. It was<i> not his choosing</i>, <b>someone</b> other changed him in to this.<br /> <br /> Happy ending is when the Beast <i>becomes </i>the Prince, not the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-27-2015, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T23:46:45-08:00","id":793457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/792605-2ed-seemings-and-fairytales?p=793446#post793446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because only &quot;curse&quot; way have logic in this story. Prince <i><b>wants to stop being</b></i> Beast - it's fundamental to this fairytale. The 2ED Seemings are this way weird, now - they are <b>totally</b> contrary to the fairytales they are based on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, your just twisting kith and seeming about. The curse isn't the seeming, it's the kith. Because of :<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Happy ending is when the Beast <i>becomes </i>the Prince, not the other way around. </div> </div> </div>Basically. He is in arcadia, he takes on the role of a noble prince right? So Prince is his original Kith. But then he does something to anger his keeper and is punished, warping him into a monstrous beast. Being a beast causes him to have the kith of Hunterheart (though could be any of the following kiths Bloodbrute/Chimera/Coldscale/Draconic/Gargantuan/etc./etc./etc. there are a lot of kiths that can represent a bestial form), and he is left in a cage of a castle. And so the tale of Beauty and the Beast begins, until he rejects his ktih in sparing the life of Gaston (a changeling on the path of the Fairest who had rallied the changelings against the beast because the keeper manipulated him into thinking that the escape was being guarded by the beast) and Gaston kills him, the beast risked everything and lost, but the Beauty saw the good within the beast enough and was inspired enough with the sacrifice the Beast made while denying his kith that his curse buckles and warps, gaining the fairest seeming, changing his form from that of a cursed beast into his true self, a strong hero.<br /> <br /> IMO, the beast should have Fairest Seeming and Hunterheart kith.<br /> <br /> The curse breaking is not him gaining a kith, his curse breaking is from him earning his seeming. It's him taking his identity back, he is not the beast that he has been portrayed as, he is a Hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 12-27-2015, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T00:08:55-08:00","id":793462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/792605-2ed-seemings-and-fairytales?p=793457#post793457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, your just twisting kith and seeming about. The curse isn't the seeming, it's the kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand 2ED spoilers getting changeling template looks like this:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Mortal is stolen or tricked by the True Fae to go to Arcadia.</li> <li>Mortal is in Durance of Gentry, developing Kith to fulfill his new purpose the Keeper has put on him. In our &quot;<i>Beauty and the Beast&quot; </i>example, some French peasant becomes Prince Kith, as he is bound to be &quot;Prince of Secret Kingdom&quot; from now on by True Fae.</li> <li>In 2ED now kidnapped revolt against his Keeper, getting Seeming by the Wyrd. He return from the Arcadia to Earth then. In our example, now Prince become Beast, changing his physics and Mein. It can be seen as &quot;cursed&quot;, but it means that our Prince <b>did not wanted</b> to get his Seeming. He did <b>not wanted to</b> be Beast.</li> <li>And then comes Belle and she goes to &quot;break the curse&quot;, in other way, take out Seeming from the character. But it means the Prince did not wanted Seeming in the first place. It means he was... Loyalist! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ol><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/792605-2ed-seemings-and-fairytales?p=793457#post793457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is in arcadia, he takes on the role of a noble prince right? So Prince is his original Kith. But then he does something to anger his keeper and is punished, warping him into a monstrous beast. Being a beast causes him to have the kith of Hunterheart (though could be any of the following kiths Bloodbrute/Chimera/Coldscale/Draconic/Gargantuan/etc./etc./etc. there are a lot of kiths that can represent a bestial form), and he is left in a cage of a castle.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not how it is shown in spoilers. From what we know character has one Kith the Keeper stole his for. Becoming Seeming ( i.e. Beast ) <b>does not </b>change your Kith. If you were of Prince Kith, you will <b>always</b> be a Prince. Your own choosing is <i>only</i> your Seeming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/792605-2ed-seemings-and-fairytales?p=793457#post793457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And so the tale of Beauty and the Beast begins, until he rejects his ktih in sparing the life of Gaston (a changeling on the path of the Fairest who had rallied the changelings against the beast because the keeper manipulated him into thinking that the escape was being guarded by the beast) and Gaston kills him, the beast risked everything and lost, but the Beauty saw the good within the beast enough and was inspired enough with the sacrifice the Beast made while denying his kith that his curse buckles and warps, gaining the fairest seeming, changing his form from that of a cursed beast into his true self, a strong hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not think character can change Kith and Seemings in such ways as you are describing. I think that much easier would be loosing you own Seeming and going in to Seemingless, than juggle on yours &quot;scars&quot; ( Seeming and Kith ).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/792605-2ed-seemings-and-fairytales?p=793457#post793457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The curse breaking is not him gaining a kith, his curse breaking is from him earning his seeming. It's him taking his identity back, he is not the beast that he has been portrayed as, he is a Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this interpretation means the whole 1ED Beast Seeming rationality is thrown out of window and exemplar fairy tale of Beasts is about Fairest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T00:23:37-08:00","id":793467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/792605-2ed-seemings-and-fairytales?p=793462#post793462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I understand 2ED spoilers getting changeling template looks like this:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Mortal is stolen or tricked by the True Fae to go to Arcadia.</li> <li>Mortal is in Durance of Gentry, developing Kith to fulfill his new purpose the Keeper has put on him. In our &quot;<i>Beauty and the Beast&quot; </i>example, some French peasant becomes Prince Kith, as he is bound to be &quot;Prince of Secret Kingdom&quot; from now on by True Fae.</li> <li>In 2ED now kidnapped revolt against his Keeper, getting Seeming by the Wyrd. He return from the Arcadia to Earth then. In our example, now Prince become Beast, changing his physics and Mein. It can be seen as &quot;cursed&quot;, but it means that our Prince <b>did not wanted</b> to get his Seeming. He did <b>not wanted to</b> be Beast.</li> <li>And then comes Belle and she goes to &quot;break the curse&quot;, in other way, take out Seeming from the character. But it means the Prince did not wanted Seeming in the first place. It means he was... Loyalist! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>IMO you got 3 and 4 wrong for my example. For mine, he didn't leave to go to earth when he was cursed. He was cursed in the middle of his durance. &quot;breaking&quot; the curse was part of the escape. Also, I've never heard of anyone being able to take a seeming away from a character, where are you getting that from?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not how it is shown in spoilers. </div> </div> </div>Not sure how it isn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what we know character has one Kith the Keeper stole his for. </div> </div> </div>There is no reason the keeper cannot change your kith at a whim, especially since they do choose what you are and have full control over your form. They can have you as a Prince, and then if you annoy them, they can punish you and turn you into an ugly monster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Becoming Seeming ( i.e. Beast ) <b>does not </b>change your Kith. </div> </div> </div>.... how did you even read that in my post. No, seeming doesn't change your kith... I never suggested it did. The seeming didn't change the kith at all in my example. He kept the kith of Hunterheart. He never even got the Beast seeming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you were of Prince Kith, you will <b>always</b> be a Prince. </div> </div> </div>Unless the keeper changes it, which is completely within their rights as your keeper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your own choosing is <i>only</i> your Seeming. </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not think character can change Kith and Seemings in such ways as you are describing. I think that much easier would be loosing you own Seeming and going in to Seemingless, than juggle on yours &quot;scars&quot; ( Seeming and Kith ). </div> </div> </div>The character didn't change seemings (he only ever got Fairest), and it'd be strange if Gentry couldn't give their changeling's kiths..... since otherwise changelings couldn't get kiths.....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And this interpretation means the whole 1ED Beast Seeming rationality is thrown out of window and exemplar fairy tale of Beasts is about Fairest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily, the beast Seeming is for the Beast at the start of the fairy tale (break the rules and become a beast), while my story gives the result of the Beast being a fairest at the end of the fairy tale (inspire people, make a sacrifice, be a hero and get your human form back from the curse). I see the durance as being from &quot;when he was taken out of his normal life&quot; to &quot;regaining his agency and sense of self&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 12-27-2015, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}